This is a large shallow bowl, probably about 24 cm across, holding a small pile of spinach leaves with a few shredded carrots. The spinach looks lightly dressed, with a slight sheen. I estimate roughly 10-15 leaves, which comes to about 40 g of spinach, plus about 5 g of carrot and some dressing. That gives a total of about 50 g.

Spinach is about 23 kcal per 100 g, so 40 g is roughly 10 kcal. Carrot adds about 2 kcal. A light dressing of about 5 g, at roughly 4 kcal per gram for an oil-based vinaigrette, adds about 20-30 kcal. The total comes to about 35-45 kcal.

